# Cooperative mapping view - the shot for evaluation criterion 1.
#
# Fixed Frame is fleet_map, because that is the frame the composited map and both
# global costmaps live in; anything else makes the two robots' scans drift apart
# on screen for reasons that have nothing to do with the mapping.
#
# WHAT IS ON BY DEFAULT
#   Fleet map (/fleet_map)                the deliverable - the composite
#   amr1/amr2 model, scan, plan           two robots, blue and amber
#   TF (key frames only)                  fleet_map -> amrN/map -> amrN/odom -> base
#
# WHAT IS OFF BY DEFAULT, AND WHY IT IS HERE
#   amr1 own map / amr2 own map           each robot's slam_toolbox output. Toggle
#                                         them on to show the composite IS a fusion
#                                         of two maps rather than one robot's map
#                                         with a second robot driving over it.
#   amr1/amr2 global costmap              the fleet map arriving as the static layer
#                                         of both planners - the "it is used, not
#                                         just published" half of the requirement.
#   amr1/amr2 predicted trajectory        the MAPF message: where each robot expects
#   amr1/amr2 local costmap               to BE, deposited as time-decayed cost in
#                                         the OTHER robot's local costmap. Turn all
#                                         four on for the Phase 6 conflict demo -
#                                         the shot is amr1's yellow predicted path
#                                         lying across amr2's local costmap.
#
# QoS is set per display and is not decoration: /fleet_map, both robots' maps and
# both costmaps are RELIABLE + TRANSIENT_LOCAL publishers, and a VOLATILE
# subscriber joining late gets nothing at all with no error anywhere.
#
# Colours: amr1 is blue (body) / green (scan, plan), amr2 is amber (body) /
# orange (scan) / cyan (plan). The body colours come from body_color in
# config/fleet.yaml - RViz's RobotModel display has no colour property.
Panels:
  - Class: rviz_common/Displays
    Help Height: 0
    Name: Displays
    Property Tree Widget:
      Expanded:
        - /Global Options1
        - /Fleet map1
        - /TF (key frames)1
      Splitter Ratio: 0.5
    Tree Height: 719
  - Class: rviz_common/Selection
    Name: Selection
  - Class: rviz_common/Views
    Expanded:
      - /Current View1
    Name: Views
    Splitter Ratio: 0.5
